{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1366302-imagine-that-a-changling-gets-green-lighted-into-a-video-game-what-do-you-want","id":1366302,"title":"imagine that a Changling: gets green-lighted into a video game. what do you want?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-08T05:45:30-08:00","id":1366302,"title":"imagine that a Changling: gets green-lighted into a video game. what do you want?","content":"so bloodlines two sells as much as GTA 5 and Paradox decides to green light a Changling game what do you want?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T13:23:35-08:00","id":1366616,"title":"","content":"Generally, I like single player RPGs with an open sandbox setting (preferably a large city with a wide variety of neighborhoods and terrains, as well as various Dreaming realms), a lot of interesting supporting characters I can get emotionally invested in and impact their character growth (including various potential romantic interests), the ability to impact the world and what happens, and a lot of various options for my character. (Yes, generally, something like Dragon Age or Mass Effect for Changeling.)<br /> <br /> It'd be nice to have something that lets you pick any of the Kiths, but I suspect for simplicity's sake you'd just have Sidhe has the default. That is, unless you had a World of Warcraft type game that lets you play any of a dozen or more &quot;races&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T02:54:43-08:00","id":1368267,"title":"","content":"I agree with the Sandbox part. VTMB was KINDA like a Sandbox but it wasn't. It was too linear. Hopefully in VTMB2 they'll make more like GTA with better free-roaming than in the first game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T01:10:58-07:00","id":1392148,"title":"","content":"Two things come immediately to mind:<br /> <br /> An option to have the game hew to the lore as much as possible. The player character experiences Chrysalis, but the player doesn't decide which Kith they are. The character attends their Saining and is given an unchangeable auto-generated True Name. Gathering and using Glamour involves choosing from the 'nice', 'not nice' and 'downright evil' options, and if you choose Rhapsody, your target is permanently destroyed as a future source of glamour.<br /> <br /> It shouldn't be the default, of course, but it should be available as an optional setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26177-frednotbob","name":"Frednotbob","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T03:12:08-07:00","id":1392165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frednotbob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1366302-imagine-that-a-changling-gets-green-lighted-into-a-video-game-what-do-you-want?p=1392148#post1392148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An option to have the game hew to the lore as much as possible. The player character experiences Chrysalis, but the player doesn't decide which Kith they are. The character attends their Saining and is given an unchangeable auto-generated True Name. Gathering and using Glamour involves choosing from the 'nice', 'not nice' and 'downright evil' options, and if you choose Rhapsody, your target is permanently destroyed as a future source of glamour.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree with you, except on the bit about not deciding which Kith you would want to play. So, you exit the Chrysalis as a River Hag, you have to reboot the game? (An interesting angle, but not one that would help Paradox sell the game, I'm afraid...)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T09:23:43-07:00","id":1392218,"title":"","content":"I think open world could by kinda hard to do. I rather have smaller maps but with actual interesting content. Changeling is a scenario where the world need to feel truly alive, not only the npcs, but every object.<br /> <br /> I think being able to toggle between Banal vision and Glamour vision could be a interesting way to show the players how the fae world works. And could also be a interesting way to divide quests between mundane and chimerical.<br /> <br /> <br /> I actually think something along the lines of the persona games could work really well, using the same structure, but pherhaps no the the turn combat. Or instead something like Disco Elysium. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T14:01:19-07:00","id":1392307,"title":"","content":"Something like Disco Elysium would be awesome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T18:43:15-07:00","id":1392378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1366302-imagine-that-a-changling-gets-green-lighted-into-a-video-game-what-do-you-want?p=1392165#post1392165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I completely agree with you, except on the bit about not deciding which Kith you would want to play. So, you exit the Chrysalis as a River Hag, you have to reboot the game? (An interesting angle, but not one that would help Paradox sell the game, I'm afraid...)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, that's why I said it should be an option, rather than the default. Besides, the player characters themselves don't know what kith they are until their Chrysalis. At most, they have vague, easily-rationalized hints...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26177-frednotbob","name":"Frednotbob","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}